<hr data-start="747" data-end="750">
<h3 data-section-id="mu3vla" data-start="752" data-end="791">❌ Why your current code looks wrong</h3>
<ul data-start="792" data-end="965">
<li data-section-id="1qgx32v" data-start="792" data-end="846">
<p data-start="794" data-end="846"><code data-start="794" data-end="813">mat-raised-button</code> has <strong data-start="818" data-end="846">default height &amp; padding</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1nvcfk8" data-start="847" data-end="894">
<p data-start="849" data-end="894"><code data-start="849" data-end="866">mat-icon-button</code> is <strong data-start="870" data-end="894">circular and shorter</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="53h193" data-start="895" data-end="965">
<p data-start="897" data-end="965">Without <code data-start="905" data-end="926">align-items: center</code>, they align to baseline → looks uneven</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="967" data-end="970">
<h3 data-section-id="qdleaq" data-start="972" data-end="1029">🚨 If you want ONLY Add button slightly up (optional)</h3>
